{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III was the count of Tripoli from 1149 to 1152. He was a member of the House of Lanfranc and the son of Roger II of Sicily. \n\n* **Birth and Early Life ** \nRaymond III was born in 1115. He was the younger brother of Roger II of Sicily and William II of Sicily. After his brothers' deaths he succeeded as count of Tripoli. He ruled over Tripoli during the Third Crusade in 1148-1149.\n\n* **Reign** \nDuring his reign Raymond III attempted to maintain his control over the city of Tripoli without the support of the Holy Roman Empire. He managed to defeat the Muslim forces in the Battle of Inab in 1149. However he was unable to capture the city of Damascus which was the key to his control over the region. \n\n* **Later Life** \nRaymond III died in 1152. He was succeeded by his brother-in-law Bohemond III of Tripoli who had married Raymond's sister. Bohemond III went on to rule over the county of Tripoli for nearly three decades.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0013606823049485683}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001284993631998077}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.9801369905471802}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.4681185781955719}, {"token": " count", "logprob": -2.1039247512817383}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0001954841281985864}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0022526620887219906}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -0.0001967951684491709}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.041704706847667694}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.028037989512085915}, {"token": "114", "logprob": -1.2015471458435059}, {"token": "9", "logprob": -0.013951397500932217}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -1.3710908889770508}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.004858711268752813}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -0.000878544058650732}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -7.712543447269127e-05}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -1.697433114